|/a-directory-to-be-working-in/and-someth|
|ing-below-that-again/workspace/agents is|
|readable to it, read-only, during its   |
|probe and at every launch, where the    |
|network is open to its vendor.          |
|Under the sandbox on Linux it starts    |
|with a private home of its own, and a   |
|sign-in made there is gone when that    |
|start ends.                             |
|Your own Antigravity uses the sign-in it|
|keeps in ~/.gemini, which another Google|
|product may share; the store release    |
|keeps a separate one. A business sign-in|
|needs the store release or a profileDir |
|you add.                                |
